2 DATE 17 JAN 1780
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fürth
3 CTRY Bayern
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham's father died on August 1, 1742.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ansbachischer Hofmünzlieferant
2 CONT
2 CONT (Lessee of the mint of the Margraviate Ansbach)
2 CONT
2 CONT né à Anspach selon Randy Schoenberg?
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT "Loew Meir Berlin's father Abraham Meir moved from Berlin to Fürth and took the name Berlin.  He must have been an ordained rabbi because Loewenstein in his 'Zur Geschichte der Juden in Fürth,' 1909, call him 'learned' and Loew is
2 CONC  called 'ben Rabbi Meir Berlin'.  He died in Fürth 1780 and was Hofmünzlieferant i.e. Court Jew of the Margrave of Ansbach.  Loewenstein says that he interceded with Emperor Josef II so that the Jews in the Prince-Bishopric of Bam
2 CONC berg were allowed to peddle.  He is mentioned in Haenle 'Geschichte der Juden im shemaligen Füurstenthuum Ansbach' (History of the Jews in the former Principality of Ansbach) as HofundKammerfactor und  Hofmünzlieferant  of Markgra
2 CONC ft Carl Alexander.  Also is he mentioned in the book by Henrich Schnee 'Die Hoffinanz und der moderne Staat' (The Court Financiers and the Modern State), Volume 4, published in Berlin 1963." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: private family history by John Josepth Thal
