1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 99	Chaim bn mvhr"r Hirsch H"X (Halberstadt) z"l, chatan Mordechai k"Ts z"l shammesh  1776
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no other record of '''Joachim''' in the registers in Prague. Perhaps ''Chaim'' and ''Joachim'' is indeed the same person. The resaon why his name is likely to have been Joachim is the second name of both his sons Markus a
2 CONC nd Löw. In the 1794 census a widow Ewa Halberstadt is mentioned with the two sons '''Markus''' and '''Löw'''. For Markus there is an extra entry in the neighbor's house with Markus and his family. Ewa's job is a Kuchenhändlerin (p
2 CONC astry seller) and Markus is a Kuchenbäcker (pastry baker). Two years before in 1792 only Markus is listed and there he is a "Kolatschen Bäcker".
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1786 there is a death record for a '''Gitel''' Halberstadt, wife of Abraham (50 years old) - house Nr 248 (hospital?) 18april1786 - PRAHA, 2753, Z 1784-1801, (R26/Fol47) - https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=600000014196
2 CONC 0146823 - also a relative?
