2 NOTE I was reminded of this matter by a fellow researcher, and reviewed my data from Otser HaRabanim, Jacobi, and Rosenstein, and have found only one piece of evidence regarding the identity of the mother of Jacob David Neumark: in Vol
3 CONC ume 1, p 36 of the Jacobi Papers, he asserts that the wife of Naphtali Hersz Neumark (Jacob David's father) is a daughter of the Bacharach family. No first name is given, nor her ancestry, so I cannot say more. However, this may b
3 CONC e a clue as to Jacob David's mother's identity.
3 CONT
3 CONT I do know that Jacobi has a handwritten draft of the Mirels-Heller-Wallerstein tree in the Jacobi Papers, housed at the National LIbrary of Israel. This document may provide further information regarding the Bacharach reference I 
3 CONC saw. I am not near the NLI so cannot access this document, but would encourage anyone interested in this matter and who can access the library to take a look, with the understanding that reading these written drafts are in English
3 CONC  and often require some form of magnification to read.
3 CONT
3 CONT I therefore agree that there is no known evidence, apart from this current Geni proposal, that Jacob David's mother is a woman (of any given name) who is the maternal granddaughter of the Maharal of Prague.
