2 CONT Bernhard Wolff (3 March 1811 – 11 May 1879) was a German media mogul. He was editor of the Vossische Zeitung, founder of the National Zeitung (1848–1938), and founder of Wolffs Telegraphisches Bureau (1849–1934), one of the first 
2 CONC press agencies in Europe and one of the three great European telegraph monopolies until the World War II-era.
