2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giacomo_Meyerbeer '''Giacomo Meyerbeer'''] (born: Jacob Liebermann Beer) (5 September 1791 – 2 May 1864) was a noted German opera composer, and the first great exponent of "grand opera." At his peak i
2 CONC n the 1830s and 1840s, he was the most famous and successful composer of opera in Europe, yet he is rarely performed today.
