1 OCCU Deutscher Geschäftsmann, Bankier, Politiker, Publizist und Amateurastronom.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} wedding: 13.9.1818 in Berlin
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wilhelm_Beer
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.britannica.com/EBchecked/topic/58408/Wilhelm-Beer
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=516&letter=B
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm Wolff Beer (4 January 1797 – 27 March 1850) was a banker and astronomer from Berlin, Prussia, and the half-brother of Giacomo Meyerbeer.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents  [show]  Astronomy[edit] Beer's fame derives from his hobby, astronomy. He built a private observatory with a 9.5 cm refractor in Tiergarten, Berlin. Together with Johann Heinrich Mädler he produced the first exact map of
2 CONC  the Moon (entitled Mappa Selenographica) in 1834-1836, and in 1837 published a description of the Moon (Der Mond nach seinen kosmischen und individuellen Verhältnissen). Both remained the best descriptions of the Moon for many de
2 CONC cades.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830, Beer and Mädler created the first globe of the planet Mars. In 1840 they made a map of Mars and calculated its rotation period to be 24 h 37 min 22.7 s, only 0.1 seconds different from the actual period as it is known tod
2 CONC ay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other work[edit] Beer was multi-talented. In addition to his hobby of astronomy, he helped with the establishment of a railway system in Prussia, and promoted the Jewish community in Berlin. In his last decade of life, he worked a
2 CONC s a writer and politician. In 1849 he was elected as an MP for the first chamber of the Prussian parliament.
2 CONT
2 CONT Named after Beer[edit] The crater Beer on Mars is named in Wilhelm Beer's honor and lies near Mädler. There is also a crater called Beer on the Moon and an asteroid 1896 Beer.
