1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ttps://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-255919161-1-535599/baerman-eliahu-samuel-fraenkel-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-519257bf8d6c6d493f632eb739aca98f&mrid=676182f7c5fc078c42ed86b92036c9
2 CONC 48
2 CONT
2 CONT The above record shows his birth date as 1653 which would seem more accurate otherwise both his parents were 12 years old
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: ''The Fränkel Family'' (a book or a chapter from a book) introduces him as follows: "Bärman Fränkel, or as was called by his Jewish name,'' Reb. Samuel Eli Jissarchar ben Isac ha-Levi''. . ."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT See article "Koppel Fraenkel and His Descendants" and pages from ''The Fränkel Family'' under the "Documents" section of the "Media" tab.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT "[David Seckel's son, Koppel Fraenkel's grandson] Eli Jissachar Baermann, when still young, became Dayan in Fuerth, then Chief Rabbi for Schnaittach and the principality of Ansbach, afterwards also Landrabbiner of the Jews of Bran
2 CONC denburg, an office which he administered from Fuerth."  From article "Koppel Fraenkel and His Descendants."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT His "greatest achievement was the founding of a Klaus synagogue in Fürth." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Read
2 CONT [https://www.fuerthwiki.de/wiki/index.php/Wiener_Memorbuch#F%C3%BCrther_Teil The Viennese Memorbuch of the Klaus Synagogue in Fürth] is a memorial book (Memor) that was written in the Jewish community in Vienna from 1633 and conti
2 CONC nued in Fürth until 1932.
2 CONT
2 CONT "When Emperor Leopold I ordered the expulsion of the Jews from Vienna, the Memorbuch came to Fürth from Vienna with the Fränkel family. The entries up to 1708 were reserved for the Fränkel family. Bärmann Fränkel, who was born in 
2 CONC Vienna and then worked as Ansbach's state rabbi, donated the Fürth Klaus Synagogue in 1708, the year of his death, in which the entries in the Memorbuch were taken up again until 1932. The first Fürth entry of 207 names Isaak Seck
2 CONC el Segal Fränkel (d. November 4, 1691), the last of whom was the rabbi of the Klaus Synagogue Markus Mordechai Leib Faust, who died on May 5, 1932. As a special feature, there are also entries of fallen Jewish soldiers from the ti
2 CONC me of the First World War."
2 CONT
2 CONT see also [https://sammlungen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/cm/periodical/titleinfo/2881259 Das Wiener Memorbuch in der Klaussynagoge von Fürth / Leopold Löwenstein 1898]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''The Fränkel Family'' says he had five sons and one daughter, Abraham, Isak, Jacob Koppel, Zacharias, Jakob Benjamin Wolf and Treinle.  The inconsistency with what currently shows on Geni is for one son - there is no "Jacob Koppe
2 CONC l," and instead there is "Benjamin Wolf Halevi Fraenkel."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Birth date above probably incorrect.  He is described in ''The Fränkel Family'' as having a short life and dying September 30, 1708 at "a young age."   
2 CONT
2 CONT né en 1660??? pour certains
