2 CONC 'Hannah/Hena bat Abraham Elieser Keijser, wife of A./Ziskind D./Daniel Abrahams/Rachmanuth', died from 'waterzucht', occupation: schoolkeeper, from: 'Joodse leerlingen op een openbare school in Amsterdam in 1823', by Harmen Snel, 
2 CONC in Misjpoge, 20, 2007,Vol 1, pp 5-11:  on 13 Sep 1808 - admission to the keeping of a small children's school  shortly afterwards depart to London and marriage in Great Synagogue there on 18 May 1813 to Alexander Daniel Abrahams, 
2 CONC businessman, born in Amsterdam.  on 14 Jan 1830 the couple makes up a testament before notary Barend Blomman in Amsterdam.  remarriage of the couple on 25 Apr 1844 (she then 60 yrs.old, he 54 yrs) in Amsterdam, because of lack of 
2 CONC recognition by Dutch authorities of synagogual marriage in London.  after her spouse's death on 19 Apr 1847 in Amsterdam, she makes up a new testament on 20 Apr 1860.  in 1823 the school keeps 66 pupils.  on 3 Sep 1849 she renounc
2 CONC es teaching.  the couple had no children.  Married 25 Apr 1844 Amsterdam Married (church) 18 May 1813 London, synagogual marriage in Great Synagogue. to:  Alexander Ziskind Daniel Abrahams Rachmanuth, birth Sep 1791 Amsterdam, 'Ci
