1 TITL Rabbi Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacobi, Vo. I, p. 178
2 CONT
2 CONT last name also: HALFANUS
2 CONT
2 CONT Admitted by Emperor Rudolf II as Physician in Wien July 5, 1598
2 CONT
2 CONT Rudolf II, Holy Roman Emperor, “Freibrief” Permission for Dr. Elias Chalfon to move from Prague to Vienna, July 5, 1598 Niedersächsisches Landesarchiv, Stade, Germany, Rep. 32 Nr. 450, formerly Cal. Br. Arch. Des. 32 I Nr. 16
2 CONT
2 CONT His grandfather Rabbi Elijah (Elia) Menachem Chalfon (Halfon) issued a Rabbinical opinion supporting the divorce of King Henry VIII. --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des alten Judenfriedhof in Wien" - Dr. Bernhard Wachstein, Band I no. 633, pg. 481 no. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des alten Judenfriedhof in Wien" - Dr. Bernhard Wachstein, Band I  No. 118 pg. 98 -------------------- Burial record:- See Bernhard Wachstein, Die Inschriften des alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien, vol. 1 p. 98.
2 CONT
