1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Here is here grave inscription at Altona. Her grave is very close to that of her husband, Rabbi M. Zalman Mirels. http://www.steinheim-institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?id=hha-3270&lang=de
2 CONT
2 CONT Text reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT פה‏‎<br/>
2 CONT ‏נטמנה אשה הגונה<br/>
2 CONT ‎‏צנועה וישרה<br/>
2 CONT מנורה ‏טהורה ‎ ‏<br/>
2 CONT ביראת י"י היא ‏נזהרה‎<br/>
2 CONT ‎חכמנית דברנית ‏<br/>
2 CONT ‎‎היא הרבנית מ' מרים‏‎<br/>
2 CONT ‎‏בת האלוף הקצין מהו"ר ‏<br/>
2 CONT ‎ ‎‏נתן פרידלנד ז"ל והיתה ‏<br/>
2 CONT ‎ ‎‏הרבנית בק"ק אלטונא‏‎<br/>
2 CONT ‎‏והמבורג נפטרה ליל‏‎<br/>
2 CONT ‎‏ב׳ ד׳ טבת ונקברה בו‏‎<br/>
2 CONT ‎‏ביום תמ״ח ל״ק תנצב״ה<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is Buried 
2 CONT
2 CONT A decent, modest and honest woman
2 CONT
2 CONT The Pure Lamp
2 CONT
2 CONT She was careful in the fear of The Lord
2 CONT
2 CONT Clever and talkative
2 CONT
2 CONT She is Rebbetzin Mrs. Miriam
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of the leader and officer
2 CONT
2 CONT Our master the late Nathan Friedland
2 CONT
2 CONT And she was The Rebbetzin at the 
2 CONT
2 CONT Holy community of Altona And Hamburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died Sunday evening 4th Tevet
2 CONT
2 CONT and was buried the same day
2 CONT
2 CONT 5448 of the small count.[ 07.12.1687]
