1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://wayback.archive-it.org/10578/20200730005742/https://www.dutchjewry.org/genealogy/ashkenazi/693.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT marriage2 https://wayback.archive-it.org/10578/20200415005256/https://www.dutchjewry.org/ashk_tim/pers/142pers.shtml https://archief.amsterdam/indexen/deeds/a6cd69de-b8dd-4bac-988f-6472c92db8fc
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruidegom Marcus Boas Bruid Simmitje Salomons diversen Eerdere man: Ries, Moses Abraham Gebeurtenis Ondertrouw Datum 17-10-1721 Amsterdam
2 CONT
2 CONT Marcus Boas, 27 yrs.old, at Uijlenburg, accompanied by father Boas Izaaks, and Simmetje Salomon, widow of Moses Abraham Ries, at Oudeschans. (on 31 Oct the 3rd bann is delayed, because the bride did not yet introduce a proof of th
2 CONC e death of her 1st husband, and neither a consent of the Weeskamer (citybody regulating orphan's rights); on 7 Nov she complied with these demands, and the 3r d bann was published on 9 Nov, the day of her 2nd marriage)
2 CONT
2 CONT from the Weeskamer: on 7 Nov 1721 declares Ijsack Salomons de Jonge, in the name of his daughter Zibbe Isaaks, widow of Moses Abraham Ries, according to a certain act passed before the parnassim of Berlin on 25 Jan 1720, stating t
2 CONC hat Zibbe Isaack s has left her three children in the care of close friends of the side of their father, which was certified there
