1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Ferdinand_Koreff
2 CONT
2 CONT David Ferdinand Koreff (after his baptism in 1816 , Johann (es) Ferdinand Koreff ; * 1 February 1783 in Breslau , † 15 May 1851 in Paris ) was a German writer and physician and member of various literary groups.
2 CONT
2 CONT Koreff came from an upper middle class Jewish family. His father Joachim Koreff Salomon (1732-1805) was a physician in Breslau and had the famous Franz Anton Mesmer known whose ideas of animal magnetism should also influence the s
2 CONC trong son. [1] from 1802 Koreff studied medicine at the University of Halle . There, he turned under the influence of Schelling to the "natural philosophy" The branch of medicine at that time by the writings of Franz von Baader wa
2 CONC s coined. Starting in 1803, he completed his clinical studies in Berlin, where he connected to the romantic North Star League to Adelbert von Chamisso and Varnhagen von Ense found. He gained access to literary salons of Berlin and
2 CONC  also joined the Serapion Brothers in, the literary circle frequented by ETA Hoffmann . In his short story collection The Serapionsbrüder Koreff is portrayed as the witty conversationalist mystical Vincent. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Paris [ Edit ] After graduating, he moved to Paris and began to practice, especially among members of the local German colony. At the same time he pursued numerous literary projects. His most important literary works were his lyri
2 CONC cal poems (1815). This includes the "prayer of a magnetizer," which is his poetic space medicine understanding expression on which a prescription and a sonnet are just "different emanations of divinity" is [3] :
2 CONT
2 CONT High out of your blissful distance Descend down, star bright, Lowers you into the human construction. As you err on the Wandrung And never the train Confused, Billowing in the sky blue! He wrote the libretto for the opera Aucassin
2 CONC  and Nicolette , an adaptation of the old French tale Aucassin et Nicolette , which was performed in 1822 in Berlin. He also worked as a translator and rendered poems of Tibullus and elegies of Sulpicia into German.
2 CONT
2 CONT Confidant Hardenberg in Berlin [ Edit ] The Congress of Vienna, he was of Wilhelm von Humboldt , whose family doctor by his acquaintance with Humboldt's wife Caroline , he was, at the Prussian chancellor Karl August von Hardenberg
2 CONC  introduced. He managed to win his trust. Hardenberg gave him first a professor at the University of Berlin . His opponents pointed out that as a Jew is not entitled to such a place had what prompted the Chancellor personally that
2 CONC  Koreff in the Lutheran Church was baptized. He also made ​​him his personal physician and confidant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Once it was possible Koreff 1817, Hardenberg to heal from a serious illness, his position was fully consolidated. He received the presentation for scientific and artistic issues in the Chancellery and was particularly with the exp
2 CONC ansion of human Humboldt University in Berlin and the establishment in 1818 of the newly founded University of Bonn deals. He succeeded, August Wilhelm Schlegel and Ernst Moritz Arndt winning professors. [4] Koreff was now at the 
2 CONC height of his career, and in the center of Berlin society and the literary Germany: He gave Ludwig Tieck and Jean Paul stately inns, made Gaspare Spontini known in Berlin and was one of Alexander von Humboldt and Hegel to his inte
2 CONC rlocutors. [5] 1818 Koreff was also a member of the nonprofit Academy Sciences in Erfurt .
2 CONT
2 CONT By him to an increased interest Hardenbergs formed on mesmerism , as Koreff practiced this technique and this sensational success - especially in the treatment of the mentally ill - attributed. As evidence of such a miraculous rec
2 CONC overy he introduced a device called Friederike Hähnel in Hardenberg's house, where she impressed the aging chancellor not only by spirit-but above all by their beauty. For this reason, they should probably the Princess Charlotte [
2 CONC 6] are added as a shareholder. This lady, however, should prove to Hardenberg's marriage as explosive. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1822, it was the loss of trust in Hardenberg, in his absence, he a font Benz's to Benjamin Constant was sent to Paris, there under his and Constant's name with the provocative title you triomphe inévitable et prochain the princ
2 CONC ipes constitutionnels s Prusse ("About the appeared imminent and inevitable triumph of constitutional principles in Prussia "). This pamphlet was neither Tsar Alexander , nor the Emperor Franz Joseph , still in Metternich nor at G
2 CONC entz ​​gentle reader, and it has been suggested the publication in which Hardenberg again as a champion of the parliamentary system was shown would be published at his instigation been. Even a denial Hardenberg found no credence b
2 CONC ecause Koreff a confidant Hardenberg and Constant with a cousin Hardenberg was married. Through this affair was Hardenberg's position seriously damaged and Koreffs Berliner career to an end. [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not true that the affair Hardenbergs with Friederike Hähnel, which the old prince made ​​her his lover and to camouflage a baron of Kimski (or Kimsky, allegedly a player [9] .) had married, had been responsible for Koreffs f
2 CONC all The Hähnel remained about the separation from his wife and Hardenberg's until his death in her arms, his mistress. [10] Prior (by Codizill of 20 April 1822) Hardenberg had her exposed even a pension for life. In addition, they
2 CONC  said to her, to have the dying Chancellor, on his recent trip to Verona led 100,000 dollars as travel funds with them, plundered thoroughly with her ​​husband. [9] She decided to noisy conversion to the Catholic faith their days 
2 CONC in Rome. [11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Last years in Paris [ Edit ] Sun Koreff moved to the end of his 1822 Berlin ambitions turn to Paris. To his friends in the French capital were the painter Eugène Delacroix , the philosopher Victor Cousin , the musician Giacomo Mey
2 CONC erbeer and great writers like Stendhal , Prosper Mérimée , Alfred de Musset , Victor Hugo and Heinrich Heine , whose physician he was. He was also the doctor that Marie Duplessis , as a model for the Lady of the Camellias by Alexa
2 CONC ndre Dumas fils and Verdi's La Traviata was immortal. He appeared on the French as a strange, quirky German dressed as the "Hoffmanneske doctor" ( le Drug hoffmannique ), helped by a well-supported by his loden red wig.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a scandal involving excessive fee claims (the case Lady Lincoln), he lost his job in 1838 in the fashionable world, and treated in his last years, the members of the Parisian middle class, with its slowly coming out of fashion 
2 CONC magnetic cures. He died penniless entirely.
2 CONT
2 CONT As intermediaries between the leading French and German literary groups Koreff was an important figure. Among other things, he suggested to the French edition of the works of ETA Hoffmann. Overall, he was a prime example of the ch
2 CONC aracteristic for many romantics vacillation between poles: scientist and writer, doctor and charlatan, Jew and Christian, German and French.
2 CONT
