1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Wulff Levin Fränkel (Tausk); Berlin d 1714; son of Berman Fränkel (Issachar Bärman Halevi)" on page II Q of Louis Fraenkel's book of Fraenkel family trees (also see page K in a different tree). But why would he be
2 CONC  called Levin if his father was Berman; Levin seems to go with Liepmann? Does Levin mean Halevi?
2 CONT
2 CONT '"Wolf Tausk aus Wien" at http://www.archive.org/stream/michaelberolzheimer_01_reel01#page/n854/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT Eli Handel (11 October 2010): I found "fraenkel (wolff tausk)" in the display name on Geni and I moved it to nickname; I don't know what it means.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edit by Edward Salier June 7, 2015:
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis Fraenkel's chart is incorrect.  Wulff Levin Fraenkel was the son of Jehuda Leib, who died July 23, 1700 in Zulz.  See: Brann, M., Geschichte der Juden in Schleisien, Vol. IV, Pg. XCVII.  I believe that Berman Fraenkel (Issac
2 CONC har Baerman Fraenkel) was the grandfather of Wulff Levin Fraenkel.  Wulff Levin Fraenkel was born around 1666 and Issachar Berman Fraenkel died March 27, 1662 in Vienna.  Therefore, proving that there is a generation missing in Lo
2 CONC uis Fraenkel's book.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobson, Jacob, "Die Judenburgerbucher der Stadt Berlin 1809-1851" Berlin 1962, Pg 92, footnote for 282 "Die Erinnerung an L.M. Wulff wurde wachgehalten durch die nach ihm bennante Lipmann Tausk Synagoge in Berlin. Der hebr. Bein
2 CONC ame der Familie war Tausk, abgeleited von der boehmischen Stadt Taus."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sinasshoh, M. M., "Die Berliner Privatsynagogen und ihre Rabbiner 1671-1971" Jerusalem, 1971, devotes a chapter to the Lippmann Tauss Synagogue. He notes that various members of the TAUSSIK family are recorded in the minutes of th
2 CONC e Berlin Jewish community (Josef Meisl, "Protokollbuch der jüdischen Gemeinde zu Berlin 1723-1854", Jerusalem, n.d.)
