3 CONT On October 8th, 1861, Elias Levy Ruben, on behalf of his mother-in-law, the widow Fanny Salinger née Borchardt, transferred to the pension office under the name of her sister, the deceased Ida Borchardt (who passed away on Februar
3 CONC y 8th, 1856, in Berlin), the sixth bond of the local state loan No. 25 Fol. 289 large No. 1000. The previously residing testator had given this bond for safekeeping to her mentioned sister and included it in her last will dated Fe
3 CONC bruary 8th, 1855. Besides the widow Salinger, there are also children of the deceased sister of the testator, Julie, Clara, and Emma, some of whom live here and some abroad.
