1 NAME Paul /Ewald/
2 GIVN Paul
2 _MARNM Ewald
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 7 DEC 1851
1 DEAT
2 DATE 14 OCT 1887
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He worked at the Monumenta Germaniae Historica, a 200 year old research institution for medieval history, https://www.mgh.de/en/mgh-about-us
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2020 they published a virtual exhibition on seven of our jewish employees (in German and in English), have a look: https://visit.mgh.de/en/jew-em
2 CONT
2 CONT From a historian at the monuments “ He worked as historian for the Monumenta, was born 7.12.1851 and died in 1887. His father was Julius Wilhelm Ewald (1811–1891), his mother Auguste, born Amelung, who died, when Paul was eight ye
2 CONC ars old. He had two brothers: Karl Anton Emil Ewald (1845–1915), who worked as a physician, and the physiologist Ernst Julius Richard Ewald (1855–1921), and one sister Johanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1886 the painter Clara Philippson (1859–1948) and died one year after the marriage. Their son Paul Peter Ewald (1888-1985)”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
