1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From a private family history by John Joseph Thal, a great grandson of Zerline Berlin:
2 CONT
2 CONT "From what I heard from some of the grandchildren of Samuel and Zerline Berlin, Samuel was a typical intellectual, very educated, but not a real go-getter.  Great-grandmother Zerline appears to have been the boss of the family.  S
2 CONC he was the daughter of a hop dealer in Gunzenhausen, a small place in the Bavaria Province of Mittelfranken.  She was not a doting grandmother, but my father was very fond of her.  Mother told me that when at the wedding the rabbi
2 CONC  said something of 'Grandmother looking down from heaven and joining . . . .' (She died shortly before), father cried."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuel and Zerline Berlin lived to celebrate their golden wedding, which was very rare in those days."
2 CONT
2 CONT See "Documents" section under the "Media" tab
