1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathan Arnstein’s father, Adam, mentions specifically in his will (dated 1785 – Nachlaesse page 301) that his granddaughter, Jitle (Judith), currently in Frankfurt, “daughter of my son Nathan”, is to have five thou
2 CONC sand gulden for her wedding.  This is poor Jitle who dies, unmarried, in 1789, and whose helpful grandmother, Hanna bt Isaac Arnstein, second wife of Sussel Kulp, gets buried next to Jitle when she dies in 1790. And when Jitle had
2 CONC  died, she was described on her tombstone as granddaughter of Sussel Kulp.
