1 NAME Joseph Akiba /Gugenheim/
2 GIVN Joseph Akiba
2 _MARNM Gugenheim
2 NICK Elijahu Joseph von Jugenheim
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1614 AND 1615
2 PLAC Frankfurt am Main, Hessen-Nassau, Preussen
2 ADDR
1 OCCU On 15 August 1614, sale of wine made by "Abraham, jew of frankfurt, son of Joseph, Jew of Jugenheim", Rabbin
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE: This is apparently the first time Guggenheim appears for the family on an Ele Toldot record.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ou Josef Frankfurter ou Elijahu/Eliahu Gugenheim ou von Jugenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT né vers 1560 selon certaines sources
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Pascal Faustini from work done by John Berkowitch Articles published in "Cercle de Genealogie Juive"
2 CONT
2 CONT Elie/Eliyahu Gugenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentionned in Fortune Tax Rolls in 1581, then diseapears several years when he lives in Jugenheim close to Mayence. In 1591, he is mentionned and represented by his brother Leib.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1598, the municipal registry mentions him as "Joseph von Jugenheim zur Flasche", brother of Abraham
2 CONT
2 CONT Document: 10 Jul 1598, Chancery of Mayence:"Joseph, Jew of Jugenheim, jew protected by the count of Nasau-Sarrebruck" creditor of 2100 florins with his brothers "Abraham jew zur Flasche in frankfurt" and Leib, jew of the same plac
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 August 1614, sale of wine made by "Abraham, jew of frankfurt, son of Joseph, Jew of Jugenheim"
2 CONT
2 CONT One bill mentions "Abraham jew "of" Jugenheim"
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also mentionned by Shlomo Ettlinger as "Abraham son of Eliyahu Josef"
2 CONT
2 CONT Ettlinger places the death of Joseph, with reservation, during the "Fettmilch" riots of 1614-1615
2 CONT
2 CONT His widdow Beile is still mentionned on the lists in 1619 and dies in 1626
2 CONT
2 CONT Ettlinger mentions in the Ele Toldot the known sons in frankfurt. The Memorbuch and the Grune buch of Worms allow us to add some more. The list is probably incomplete as we do not know any daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The sons who stayed in Frankfurt bear the name of their house, but the Mayer in Bingen and Akiba in Worms will carry the name Gugenheim
2 CONT
2 CONT As Maier, parnas in Bingen has no known son, his brother Akiba is the ancestor of the Gugenheim name in Worms, in Switzerland (Lengnau-Endingen), in Alsace and in Metz during the following centuries
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Heinzelmann found the notarized documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT In The Guggenheims The making of an american dynasty, Harvey O'Connor says (in 1937):
2 CONT
2 CONT The pre-Guggenheims wandered fron city to city. Perhaps they stayed a while in th village of Guggenheimb, now called Jugenheim, on the Bergstrasse between Darmstadt and Heildelberg. Who can ever know? But the name, or its variants
2 CONC , Guggenheimer, Guckenheim, Guckenheimer, Gougenheim, stuck to "die Juden von Guggenheimb"
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan A. Guggenheim 
2 CONT
2 CONT                   **********************************************
2 CONT
