2 NOTE I am not a specialist neither in Hebrew/Yiddish, nor in history of Hasidim at all, but it looks like the prevalent spelling is Horodenker, he:הורודנקר; with "ו" instead of  "נ"; from Городенка (translation: en:Horodenka, he:הורדנק
3 CONC א, yi: האראדענקא).
3 CONT Dmitry
