1 NOTE {geni:about_me} am achtzehnten September dieses Jahres, des Abends um Acht Uhr ist dem Herrn Banquier Meyer Sussmann hieselbst von dessen Gattin eine Tochter geboren die den Nahmen Jette erhalten hat.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=KQoAMuuKCZQC&pg=PA110&lpg=PA110&dq=s%C3%BC%C3%9Fmann+familie+j%C3%BCdische+halberstadt&source=bl&ots=_PeqXlf5UN&sig=ACfU3U0ZDar9kUzVZkK9T2bf0hiJ5Kg9YQ&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiC2KaF64TqAhUytTEKHbMV
2 CONC BKA4ChDoATACegQICBAB#v=onepage&q=su%C3%9Fmann&f=false Possibly him. P.110 "Sußmann"]
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly him. P.41 (#516 - keyword: Handlungshaus Süßmann)
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=CNrbyEebB5QC&pg=PA461&lpg=PA461&dq=friederike+susmann+halberstadt&source=bl&ots=AEQBta_Nhc&sig=ACfU3U03mUC9kKqiAOQ62KvBrdNuDXBtfA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjD_bGFn4zqAhVOlXIEHUFoAq0Q6AEwBHoECAgQAQ#v=
2 CONC onepage&q=friederike%20susmann%20halberstadt&f=false Jüdische Trauungen in Berlin 1759 bis 1813 S.461]
2 CONT
2 CONT Help from a Facebook genealogist, referring to Trauunungen in Berlin: "I looked it up. Sussmann Heinemann is not mentioned in the book again (as far as I can tell). To my understanding "Nr. 22" refers to the community in Halbersta
2 CONC dt. Jacobson used lists (Schutzjudenlisten) from Halberstadt (1731-1759, and 1803), although I could not find the exact reference of "Ord. Halberstadt". However, apparently it refers to a list of "Ordinäre Schutzjuden" in that com
2 CONC munity. "anges. [...] als 2. K." means "angesetzt als 2. Kind". This is of importance, since usually only the first child was allowed to settle down. This must have been an exemption."
