1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathan Israel was the founder of the well known Nathan Israel Department Store. Founded in 1815 it became one of the largest retail stores in Europe and, by 1925, employed over 2,000 workers. During the rise of Naz
2 CONC i Germany, he and his family were forced out of the business.. In 1938 the ownership of the store was given to Emil Koster, who was of non-Jewish descent. When displaying images of Kristallnacht, one of the most infamous pictures 
2 CONC is, unfortunately, that of the Nathan Israel Department Store being vandalized by mobs.
