2 DATE 25 APR 1765
2 PLAC Breslau
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Royal prussian court agent (Hofagent), merchant banker and co-owner of "Gebr. Kuh" in Breslau, community eldest With the help of their relatives Ephraim in Berlin, the Kuhs became a leading Jewish family of Breslau
2 CONC  and their fortune was estimated ca. 350.000 Reichstaler (then the worth of a county).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources''' for his ancestry, descendants, wife etc.: "Familienpapiere Kuh" Centrum Judaicum Archivium, Berlin; Familienstammbuch der Breslauer jüdischen Gemeinde, 1791; several documents from the States Archive Wroclaw; B. Bril
2 CONC ling, Geschichte der Juden in Breslau 1960-71; Selma Stern, Der preussische Staat und die Juden, 1971-75
2 CONT
2 CONT Foto: Tombstone of Abraham Kuh at the Jewish Cemetery Breslau-Claassenstrasse (destroyed, schematic drawing by Alfred Grotte, 1937)
