1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eintrag im »Gedenkbuch« des Bundesarchivs:
2 CONT
2 CONT Silbergleit, Margarete
2 CONT
2 CONT geborene Senator geboren am 04. August 1866 in Berlin / - / Stadt Berlin wohnhaft in Berlin (Tiergarten)
2 CONT
2 CONT Deportation: ab Berlin 05. August 1942, Theresienstadt, Ghetto 26. September 1942, Treblinka, Vernichtungslager
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Margarete Silbergleit nee Senator was born in 1866. Prior to WWII she lived in Berlin, Germany. Margarete perished in Minsk, Belorussia (USSR). This information is based on a List of victims from Germany found in the Gedenkbuch - 
2 CONC Opfer der Verfolgung der Juden unter der nationalsozialistischen Gewaltherrschaft in Deutschland 1933-1945, Bundesarchiv (German National Archives), Koblenz 1986
2 CONT
2 CONT and another report states:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margarethe Silbergleit nee Senator was born in 1866. During the war she was deported with Transport I/38 from Berlin to Terezin mala pevnost on 05/08/1942. Deported with Transport Br from Terezin to Treblinka on 26/09/1942. Margar
2 CONC ethe perished in the Shoah. This information is based on a List of Theresienstadt camp inmates found in the Terezinska Pametni Kniha/Theresienstaedter Gedenkbuch, Terezinska Iniciativa, vol. I-II Melantrich, Praha 1995, vol. III A
2 CONC cademia Verlag, Prag 2000
