1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Elise Herz, née von Lämel (1788-1868) was Prague-born Austrian philanthropist. Her father was the merchant Simon von Lämel. Her home in Prague was an intellectual center; however, upon her husband's death in 1850,
2 CONC  she moved to Vienna. There she was made an honorary member of the Jewish community.  Herz founded the Children's Asylum in Jerusalem, mainly for Jewish children, but a few Christian and Muslim children were accepted as well. Ludw
2 CONC ig August Frankl was commissioned to organize it." [ http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elise_Herz ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Per RootsWeb site: http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=REG&db=lorenfamily&id=I52697: "Elise Edle von LÄMEL was born 20 DEC 1788 in Prague [Bohemia] (Czech Republic) and died 25 JUL 1868 in Wien. She married Heinrich
2 CONC  HERZ, born ABT 1785, died 27 AUG 1849 in Prague."
2 CONT
2 CONT WÄHRINGER FRIEDHOF, Wien: '''Herz, Elise'''  b. 12/20/1788 	80 Year(s)  d. 07/25/1868 	bur. 12/19/1941 	WÄHRINGER FRIEDHOF 	5 		15
